# Vendored catalogue art is **committed**, not ignored — see docs/DECISIONS.md
# (2026-08-28). The rule that once stood here compared 475 images against fairy's 207 and
# concluded this set was the heavier one. It is not: 446 distinct files at 9.6 MB, against
# fairy's 207 at 27 MB. Weighing the file count rather than the bytes reversed the
# comparison, and the cost of ignoring them was a production site that served no art at all
# — `/icons/*.webp` fell through to the SPA catch-all and answered `text/html` with a 200,
# so every image failed and `CatalogueIcon` hid it exactly as designed.
#
# `cd backend && python -m scripts.download_icons` remains the reproduction, and
# `--check` remains the audit.

# A user's own GOOD export — their account data, and derivable from the game.
# Kept out of the repo for the same reason icons are: a repository is not a data store,
# and this one is personal.
references/*.json

# Screenshots passed in during review. Ignored for the same reason as the export above and
# then some: two of the first three showed the owner's own inventory, and a screenshot is
# permanent history for a conversation that is not. The *design* references this repo cites
# — `mitya*.png`, and GO's card in `docs/DECISIONS.md` — are committed deliberately and
# named here so the rule cannot swallow them.
references/*.png
!references/mitya.png
!references/mitya_ornament.png
!references/genshin_optimizer_artifact_info.png

# Screenshots from `cd backend && python -m scripts.shoot`. Working output, not artefacts.
screenshots/
